WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:15.244
The next day Pollyanna went to Sunday school after the church service.

2
00:00:17.444 --> 00:00:19.825
As she started to walk home, she spotted Dr.

3
00:00:19.865 --> 00:00:22.626
Chilton. He offered her a ride.

4
00:00:22.646 --> 00:00:27.327
"Mr. Pendleton wants you to visit him this afternoon," Dr.

5
00:00:27.347 --> 00:00:29.928
Chilton said as Pollyanna settled into the carriage.

6
00:00:31.232 --> 00:00:32.813
"He said it was very important."

7
00:00:34.073 --> 00:00:34.994
Pollyanna nodded.

8
00:00:35.014 --> 00:00:37.055
"Yes, I'll be there."

9
00:00:37.075 --> 00:00:40.876
"You seemed to upset my patient yesterday."

10
00:00:41.917 --> 00:00:43.297
The doctor's eyes twinkled.

11
00:00:43.317 --> 00:00:46.518
"I'm not sure you should go after all."

12
00:00:48.739 --> 00:00:49.660
Pollyanna laughed.

13
00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.721
"Oh, it wasn't me.

14
00:00:52.061 --> 00:00:53.001
It was Aunt Polly."

15
00:00:53.021 --> 00:00:55.342
"Your aunt!"

16
00:00:55.662 --> 00:00:56.623
Dr. Chilton said.

17
00:00:57.883 --> 00:00:59.304
Pollyanna bounced on the seat.

18
00:01:00.144 --> 00:01:03.346
"It's so exciting, just like a story in a book.

19
00:01:04.907 --> 00:01:08.889
Mr. Pendleton said not to mention it, but he won't mind if you know.

20
00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:12.151
He meant I shouldn't mention it to Aunt Polly.

21
00:01:13.412 --> 00:01:16.934
Of course, he'll want to tell her himself because that's what sweethearts do."

22
00:01:16.954 --> 00:01:23.318
"Sweethearts!" At that word the horse started violently, as if Dr.

23
00:01:23.358 --> 00:01:24.799
Chilton had jerked the reins.

24
00:01:24.819 --> 00:01:30.561
"Yes, Nancy told me that Aunt Polly had a sweetheart years ago.

25
00:01:31.842 --> 00:01:34.463
But they quarreled and broke off their engagement.

26
00:01:35.604 --> 00:01:38.405
We just figured out who Aunt Polly's sweetheart is.

27
00:01:39.005 --> 00:01:39.625
It's Mr.

28
00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:43.027
Pendleton!" "Really?

29
00:01:43.627 --> 00:01:44.808
I hadn't heard that."

30
00:01:45.528 --> 00:01:47.128
Dr. Chilton looked amused.

31
00:01:48.749 --> 00:01:52.111
They were almost at the Harrington house, so Pollyanna hurried to finish.

32
00:01:52.131 --> 00:01:54.972
"I'm so glad now.

33
00:01:56.232 --> 00:01:59.613
Everything has turned out perfectly just like in a book.

34
00:02:01.014 --> 00:02:03.174
Mr. Pendleton asked me to come live with him.

35
00:02:04.135 --> 00:02:07.396
But I can't leave Aunt Polly after all she's done for me.

36
00:02:08.496 --> 00:02:12.397
Then he told me about the woman he used to love and that he still loves her.

37
00:02:14.218 --> 00:02:17.319
So Aunt Polly and I will go live with him, or he'll come live with us."

38
00:02:19.999 --> 00:02:21.360
Pollyanna paused for breath.

39
00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:27.123
"We haven't got everything settled yet, so I suppose that's why he wants to see me later."

40
00:02:27.143 --> 00:02:31.766
"Hmm, yes, well, here we are at your house."

41
00:02:34.227 --> 00:02:36.229
Dr. Chilton pulled his horse to a stop.

42
00:02:37.189 --> 00:02:38.750
"There's Aunt Polly in the window!"

43
00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:40.011
Pollyanna cried.

44
00:02:44.013 --> 00:02:45.034
now I don't see her."

45
00:02:46.315 --> 00:02:47.976
The doctor was no longer smiling.

46
00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:56.381
That afternoon Pollyanna found a nervous Mr.

47
00:02:56.401 --> 00:02:58.002
Pendleton waiting in his library.

48
00:02:58.022 --> 00:03:02.684
"I've been thinking about this ever since you left yesterday," he said.

49
00:03:02.704 --> 00:03:07.246
"Why did you say I wanted Aunt Polly's hand and heart years ago?"

50
00:03:07.266 --> 00:03:11.187
"Because you were sweethearts!

51
00:03:12.048 --> 00:03:14.529
And I was so glad you still felt that way."

52
00:03:14.549 --> 00:03:17.910
"Sweethearts? Your aunt and me?"

53
00:03:19.571 --> 00:03:22.072
Pollyanna was startled by the surprise in his voice.

54
00:03:23.308 --> 00:03:24.569
"Nancy said you were."

55
00:03:24.589 --> 00:03:27.430
"Nancy was wrong."

56
00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:30.932
"You mean, you weren't engaged?"

57
00:03:31.313 --> 00:03:32.894
Pollyanna said with dismay.

58
00:03:32.914 --> 00:03:35.975
"Never." Mr.

59
00:03:36.035 --> 00:03:37.456
Pendleton stared out the window.

60
00:03:37.476 --> 00:03:42.879
"But everything was working out perfectly just like in a book."

61
00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.341
Pollyanna was on the verge of tears.

62
00:03:46.361 --> 00:03:50.944
"I'd have been glad to live here—with Aunt Polly."

63
00:03:53.056 --> 00:03:55.078
Mr. Pendleton didn't look at Pollyanna.

64
00:03:55.098 --> 00:03:57.839
"Does that mean you won't come now?"

65
00:03:57.859 --> 00:03:59.981
"I can't.

66
00:04:00.481 --> 00:04:01.742
I'm Aunt Polly's."

67
00:04:03.363 --> 00:04:09.107
The man turned toward Pollyanna and said fiercely, "Before you were hers, you were your mother's.

68
00:04:10.248 --> 00:04:12.930
And it was your mother's hand and heart that I wanted years ago."

69
00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:16.232
"My mother's?"

70
00:04:17.233 --> 00:04:18.214
Pollyanna blinked.

71
00:04:19.114 --> 00:04:21.076
She couldn't believe what she was hearing.

72
00:04:22.844 --> 00:04:25.426
"I loved your mother, but she didn't love me.

73
00:04:26.587 --> 00:04:29.770
Instead she married your father, and my whole world collapsed.

74
00:04:31.632 --> 00:04:36.636
I became a grumpy, unlovable, unloved old man—although I'm not yet sixty.

75
00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:42.160
Then one day you danced into this gray, stone house like a colorful prism.

76
00:04:43.982 --> 00:04:47.765
At first, I couldn't stand to be reminded of your mother, but that's changed.

77
00:04:48.986 --> 00:04:51.148
Now I'm begging you to let me adopt you."

78
00:04:52.748 --> 00:04:54.950
Pollyanna's eyes blurred with tears.

79
00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:56.952
"But, Mr.

80
00:04:57.052 --> 00:04:59.614
Pendleton, what about Aunt Polly?"

81
00:05:01.836 --> 00:05:03.958
Mr. Pendleton gestured impatiently.

82
00:05:03.978 --> 00:05:05.599
"What about me?

83
00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:07.361
How can I be glad without you?

84
00:05:08.282 --> 00:05:10.764
I'll spend every last cent of my money on your happiness."

85
00:05:12.065 --> 00:05:13.346
Pollyanna looked shocked.

86
00:05:13.366 --> 00:05:17.290
"But you've saved your money for the orphans overseas."

87
00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:22.501
"I never Pollyanna didn't notice that Mr.

88
00:05:22.541 --> 00:05:23.921
Pendleton had tried to speak.

89
00:05:23.941 --> 00:05:26.483
"And you make people like Mrs.

90
00:05:26.603 --> 00:05:30.224
Snow and Nancy glad with your gifts," she went on.

91
00:05:31.485 --> 00:05:33.025
Mr. Pendleton shook his head.

92
00:05:33.045 --> 00:05:35.967
"Prisms and a gold coin—they're nothing.

93
00:05:37.167 --> 00:05:39.408
And Miss Polly doesn't need you as much as I do."

94
00:05:39.428 --> 00:05:45.931
"I know she's glad—" "Miss Polly doesn't know how to be glad about anything.

95
00:05:46.971 --> 00:05:48.632
She only knows how to do her duty.

96
00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:51.846
Please, just ask if she'll let you live here."

97
00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:56.959
Pollyanna promised to ask, but she wasn't very glad about it!
